Review probes (PR #314, Review R): forms that hid an import from the lexer
while the node was reported verified, plus lexer controls. A "/" whose
goal (regular expression or division) needs a parser, after a function or
class expression "}", a labelled block or a contextual keyword used as an
identifier, makes the file unverified; a property named like a keyword
(o.if) is decided and the import is found. A hashbang holding a quote, a
byte order mark before a hashbang, escapes and nested templates still find
the import. A file importing itself is a cycle.
